linuxmuster-radius (7.3.1) lmn73; urgency=medium

  * SECURITY: the LDAPS link to the DC is now verified. Up to 7.3.0 the stunnel
    that carries rlm_ldap's group lookup accepted any DC certificate, so an
    on-path attacker between the RADIUS VM and the DC could answer the per-SSID
    role gate and the VLAN decision (MSCHAPv2 itself runs over the signed winbind
    channel and was not affected). New instances on ldaps:// must pin the DC's
    CA: `lmnradius create --ldap-ca /etc/linuxmuster/ssl/cacert.pem` (the
    linuxmuster CA, now also written by provision-radius-account.sh as
    ldap-ca.pem) or, as the documented fallback, `--ldap-ca-tofu` (pins what the
    DC serves now, prints the SHA-256 fingerprints, warns loudly). The API
    refuses ldaps:// without a CA. A wrong CA fails closed: the container does
    not start (verified on the lab DC).
  * REQUIRED UPGRADE STEP: instances created with 7.3.0 or earlier keep running
    but unverified; `lmnradius list` and `lmnradius health` warn with
    "LDAPS unverified" until you run
    `lmnradius set-ldap-ca <instance> --ldap-ca <cacert.pem>` (or --ldap-ca-tofu).
    The command pins the CA and restarts the container with verification.
  * The domain join no longer registers the container's Docker bridge address
    (172.17.0.x) as the A record of the RADIUS FQDN: the join runs with
    --no-dns-updates and the container registers the host's LAN address (HOST_IP,
    auto-detected, `host_ip:` in config.yml overrides) on every start, so an
    upgraded host corrects its record by itself. The registration uses the
    machine account and falls back to the join credentials when the DNS node
    belongs to another account -- which is what a re-created instance hits: the
    tombstoned node of the machine account the previous `rm` deleted. Needs the
    new image, which update-all applies during the upgrade.
  * `lmnradius rm` now leaves the domain: it removes the DNS A record and deletes
    the computer account (image action `leave`, join credentials), then removes
    the container, the machine-account volume, the rendered config and the
    record. A failed leave (DC unreachable) is reported with the manual cleanup
    steps and exit 1; certs/<instance>/ is kept on purpose.
  * `--client-subnet` inside 127.0.0.0/8 (or any CIDR covering 127.0.0.1) is
    rejected: loopback is the image's healthcheck client and such a client made
    the instance crash-loop while create/reconcile still reported "running".
  * create/reconcile/status report the container honestly: `running` is false
    while Docker restarts it, `crash_looping` + `restart_count` + `last_error`
    (the entrypoint's FATAL line) flag a restart loop; create and reconcile wait
    up to 45 s for healthy/crash and exit 1 when the instance is not running.
    The updater treats a crash loop as a failed update and rolls back at once.
  * The instance change log works: the postinst initialises and configures the
    git repository as the service user (it did so as root after the chown, git
    refused, the identity was never set and every commit failed silently), sets
    user.name/user.email in the repo, and on upgrade commits records that were
    only ever staged. The service commits with an explicit identity; a git
    failure is now an error (HTTP 500 with git's message) instead of silence.
  * The .deb ships DEBIAN/md5sums (dpkg --verify works, lintian
    no-md5sums-control-file is gone).
  * Renovate also bumps the pinned types-PyYAML (four-part version) in ci.yml;
    install.md aborts with a message when the GitHub API returns no version.
  * docs: stray </content></invoke> lines removed from radius-and-ad.md;
    LDAPS verification, DNS registration and the rm teardown documented
    (radius-and-ad.md, threat-model.md, operations.md, install.md); eapol_test
    recipe (package eapoltest, -N30, no -d on Ubuntu) added to install.md;
    discover-ad-facts.sh now emits the recommended role-teacher/role-student
    skeleton with all-wifi for multi-school setups; --passphrase mentioned in
    certs-and-ca.md.

 -- Kevin Stenzel <mail@kevin-stenzel.de>  Tue, 22 Sep 2026 15:00:00 +0200

linuxmuster-radius (7.3.0) lmn73; urgency=medium

  * Switch to the linuxmuster.net version scheme (7.<line>.<n>, distribution lmn73).
  * debian/changelog is the single version source: the .deb, the Python package
    and GET /v1/version all report it (no more hand-edited version in four files).
  * Add `lmnradius test <instance> [--user <name>]`: domain-login diagnostics
    from the console. Without --user a winbind trust check (the "machine account
    deleted" case); with --user one real ntlm_auth MSCHAPv2 run (password + wifi
    gate, exactly the server's mschap path) plus a per-SSID gate preview.
    NT_STATUS_* codes are translated, --json for scripts, exit code as the
    assertion; the password is prompted hidden and never logged or stored. New
    endpoint POST /v1/instances/{name}/test with strict username validation.
  * `lmnradius logs` prints real log lines instead of a JSON blob with escaped
    newlines; --json keeps the wrapped form for scripts.
  * Security fix for servers upgraded from 0.1.6 or earlier: the postinst now
    clears the group/world write bits under /opt/linuxmuster-radius on every
    configure. Those releases shipped that tree world-writable; an upgrade reset
    the files but left 421 directories at 0777 -- among them the venv's
    site-packages, where any local user could drop a .pth file that then executes
    as lmnradius, who is in the docker group.
  * Quieter auth log: the stunnel LDAP-TLS terminator runs at debug=4 (warnings
    and errors only); takes effect with the next image update.
  * Add `make deb`; CI builds the package in ghcr.io/linuxmuster/lmndev-runner:24.04
    and install-smokes it on ubuntu-24.04; a tag v<version> releases it after a
    tag == changelog gate (replaces build-deb.yml).
  * Unify the maintainer address to Kevin Stenzel <mail@kevin-stenzel.de>.
  * docs: linuxmuster-import-devices deletes any machine account without a
    devices.csv row, which kills every login until `lmnradius restart` re-joins;
    register the RADIUS VM in devices.csv. install.md no longer hard-codes a
    release version and calls the real-world deployment a pilot.

